# Shared review rooms — notes

## Architecture
- `src/teams.ts` (mounted from `src/index.ts`): team, membership, team-upload and room-handshake routes. All sit behind the existing `requireAuth` (signed cookie + D1 session row, so logout takes effect immediately) and the existing same-origin check for non-GET methods.
- Membership lives in D1 (`migrations/0002_teams.sql`: `teams`, `team_members`, `team_uploads`; existing migrations untouched). Every request queries `team_members` directly; there is no authorization cache.
- Team files are stored in R2 under `teams/<teamId>/<server-generated uuid>`; the D1 row is looked up by `(id, team_id)`, so an ID from another team resolves to nothing. Bodies are bounded while streaming (`readBounded`), so chunked uploads are cut off at 1 MiB with 413. Personal `/api/uploads` is unchanged.
- `src/room.ts`: `Room`, a SQLite Durable Object per `teamId:room`, using the hibernation API (`acceptWebSocket`, `serializeAttachment`, `webSocketMessage`/`Close`/`Error`). Messages go into a `messages` table (`AUTOINCREMENT` seq, so it never repeats after pruning) before being broadcast. The last 500 rows are kept; new sockets get the latest 50. `ping` is answered with `pong` through `setWebSocketAutoResponse`.
- The DO is only reachable through the membership-checked Worker route. The Worker builds a fresh header set (client identity headers are dropped) and adds `X-Verified-User` and a lease expiry. There is no other forwarding or admin endpoint.
- Authorization lease: min(now + 5 min, session expiry), stored in the socket attachment. After it passes, the next message (or broadcast) closes that socket with 1008, and the client must reconnect through a fresh handshake.
- `public/teams.html`: UI using the `data-testid` controls from the spec. Text is rendered with `textContent`; reconnecting closes the previous socket first, and a generation counter ignores events from superseded sockets.

## Follow-up: viewers, live authorization, retry-safe messages
- **Roles**: `owner`, `member`, `viewer`. `migrations/0003_viewer_role.sql` rebuilds `team_members` (SQLite can't alter a CHECK), copying every existing row; `0001`/`0002` and the DO migration tag `v1-rooms` are untouched. Viewers may list teams, connect, read history/live messages and download files; uploads, deletes and membership changes return 403. The owner stays immutable (409).
- **Live authorization**: socket attachments hold identity only (user, team, session id, connection id). On every send the Room queries D1 once (session not revoked/expired joined to current membership) for the sender and all connected sockets *before* committing. Removed/logged-out senders get `{type:"error",code:"unauthorized"}` and the socket is closed (1008); viewers get `code:"forbidden"` and nothing is committed. Recipients without current authority are skipped and closed. Commit, dedupe lookup and fanout then run in one synchronous block, so ordering and per-send authorization hold. The five-minute lease is gone from the DO; D1 is the authority. Sockets opened before this change have no session id and are closed on their next send (they reconnect). If D1 is unreachable the send is refused (`code:"unavailable"`).
- **clientId**: optional `[A-Za-z0-9_-]{1,80}`. Stored in a new additive DO table `client_ids (user_id, client_id, text, seq)`, separate from `messages`, so old rooms need no rewrite and records survive pruning and restarts. The authority check runs before the dedupe lookup. Exact retry → `{type:"ack",seq,clientId}` to the retrying socket only; different text → `{type:"error",code:"conflict",clientId}`. Message events and snapshots include `clientId` when one was supplied. Errors now carry a `code` next to the existing `error` string.
- **UI**: viewers get `message-send`, `message-text` and `team-upload` disabled after team selection; a role change shows after reload. Each send uses a fresh UUID `clientId`; the page never resends automatically after reconnect.

## Commands
`pnpm run typecheck`, `pnpm test`, `pnpm run build`, `pnpm run db:local` (or the project check tools).

## Limitations
- An idle socket of a removed/logged-out user is only closed when the next send in that room triggers the authority check; it receives nothing from sends made after the revocation. Events already queued or authorized before the revoking response may still be delivered.
- Dedupe records are kept forever (one small row per distinct clientId); there is no compaction. The sender-side D1 round trip adds latency per message.
- Role changes are not pushed to the UI; it needs a reload.
- Delivery is at-least-best-effort: there is no replay or exactly-once guarantee. A client that misses a broadcast sees it in the next snapshot, within the latest 50.
- Room history is pruned to the last 500 messages. Oversized frames (> 4096 bytes) close the socket (1009); other invalid input gets an `error` event.
- Membership management is API-only, and only the two demo accounts can be added. Only the `member` role can be assigned.
- If a team upload's metadata insert fails after the R2 write, the object is orphaned (no cleanup job).
- Restart persistence of room history relies on Durable Object SQLite storage and was not exercised in an automated test.
